You're a trader, but this task is a pure `goTo` job — the trading README is only context, not work to do. Two constraints to honor from the code: `await` the helper (its Outcome needs the await), and keep a wall-clock loop honest with `stopped()` — no `while(true)`, so the retry loop exits on backoff, status, or the stop flag.

Note the two Outcome fields I'm branching on — `status: 'failed'` retries, `'refused'` returns at once, `'done'` stops the loop. Exponential backoff via `setTimeout` (ms).

```ts
import {goTo, note, stopped, Outcome} from 'play';

export default async function main() {
  const target = 'sol_belt';
  const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6;   // 1 original + 5 retries

  let last: Outcome<unknown> = await goTo(target);

  if (last.status === 'refused') {
    note(`${target}: trip refused (${last.why ?? 'no reason given'}); not retrying a refusal`);
    return last;
  }

  for (let attempt = 1; attempt < MAX_ATTEMPTS; attempt++) {
    if (stopped()) {
      note(`stopped while retrying the trip to ${target}`);
      return last;
    }
    if (last.status !== 'failed') {
      note(`${target}: attempt ${attempt} ended ${last.status}; stopping retries`);
      return last;
    }

    const backoffMs = Math.pow(2, attempt - 1) * 1000;  // 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s
    note(`${target}: attempt ${attempt} failed (${last.why ?? 'no reason given'}); backing off ${backoffMs}ms`);
    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, backoffMs));

    if (stopped()) {
      note(`stopped after the ${backoffMs}ms backoff before retry ${attempt}`);
      return last;
    }

    last = await goTo(target);
  }

  if (last.status === 'done') {
    note(`${target}: arrived after ${MAX_ATTEMPTS} attempt(s)`);
  } else {
    note(`${target}: all ${MAX_ATTEMPTS} attempt(s) used, last was ${last.status} (${last.why ?? 'no reason given'})`);
  }
  return last;
}
```

The loop re-enters only when the previous attempt was `failed`, so a `refused` (returned above) and a `done` (returned inside the loop) never retry. `stopped()` is checked before each backoff and before each retry so the run can honor a stop between attempts. Each iteration ends with the last `goTo` Outcome, and the final `return last` hands back whatever the most recent attempt produced.

